From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:40:22 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 175/207] runner trace: runner_trace_check (opt-in per request)
 puts residues mod 9 and 1000 after the owned line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A request's runner_trace_check: true appends ' check: <each literal's residue> ≡ <the value's> (mod 9), ... (mod 1000)'
after the trace line when its display is decimal literals with + - * ^ and brackets (at most 4 literals, powers at
most 4) or such a divmod (q*B + r ≡ A). The residues come from the engine's value; a value its own residues contradict
is not owned. Off (the default) the line's bytes are unchanged. TraceAsk moves to runner_trace.zig (Ask).

(cherry picked from commit 75119f4094de7de3a1b8eba81d27520efdb9c8d9)
